  "findingDetails": [
    "Profiles existed only in AiWorkspace memory, so their metadata disappeared after restart. Page state did not persist its profile, and createPage chose the currently selected workspace profile.",
    "Isolated partition names omitted the vault ID and used predictable site-N IDs, permitting the same partition to be reused across vaults in one Obsidian profile.",
    "There was no connected profile rename/delete workflow or per-profile site permission store."
  ],
  "implementation": [
    "Persist validated account metadata and isolated-account grants with DurableState in .nand/browser/<device-id>/profiles.json. Read failures fail module activation without replacing the file; failed edits retain the previous durable profile and can retry.",
    "Keep the exact original default partition persist:nand-browser-<vault-id>; isolated partitions include vault and UUID profile identity. Cookies stay in Electron sessions.",
    "Persist profileId in workbench stateKeys and page state. Each guest freezes its account and has a runtime generation ID; new-window links, modal-to-tab and popout rebuild preserve the account. URL reuse also matches the profile.",
    "Expose registered BROWSER_PROFILES service and native account create/rename/open/delete controls. Selecting an account opens a new page instead of rebinding a running guest.",
    "Deletion verifies the confirmed page set, persists a deleting state, closes live/pending/saved account pages, clears only that native session, and removes metadata. Interrupted deletion can retry and rejects new pages. Module disposal stops subsequent deletion steps and drains owned operations.",
    "Add minimal shell closeResource capability to close kept resource pages without activating their browser guest. Account controls wrap at narrow widths, use 32/44px targets, and retain drafts through live language changes."
  ],
